# Recovery training from placed lying starts against a hidden get-up reference (RECOVERY.md) on absolute.args, with
# the values of BM's recovery recipe. "BM's reading of StableMimic" marks a value BM's recipe attributes to StableMimic
# (arXiv 2608.02385v1); "BM's choice" marks a value BM chose.
@absolute.args
# BM's reading of StableMimic: tracking and recovery starts are drawn equally often.
--recovery-share 0.5
# BM's choice: the get-up recordings of the 40-clip library that BM kept as hidden clips (fallAndGetUp1_subject4 is
# not among them, and is excluded from the commands below).
--recovery-hidden-clips fallAndGetUp1_subject1 fallAndGetUp1_subject5 fallAndGetUp2_subject2 fallAndGetUp2_subject3
    fallAndGetUp3_subject1
# BM's choice: no command row of a recovery start comes from a get-up recording.
--recovery-command-excluded-clips fallAndGetUp1_subject1 fallAndGetUp1_subject4 fallAndGetUp1_subject5
    fallAndGetUp2_subject2 fallAndGetUp2_subject3 fallAndGetUp3_subject1
# BM's choice: StableMimic's fall rule as BM applied it to the reference pelvis, a row is low below 0.50 m or with the
# pelvis up axis tilted beyond 60 degrees (world z below 0.5).
--recovery-low-pelvis 0.50 0.5
# BM's choice: a get-up ends at the last row of its first 1 s (50 rows) of upright rows; at most 7.5 s (375 rows) from
# a start row to that end, so the blend and 1 s of command tracking fit the 10 s episode; a command row has 500 upright
# rows ahead inside its clip (the episode limit), so no clip end or low command meets a recovery episode.
--recovery-rows 50 375 500
# BM's reading of StableMimic: the get-up tracking terms weigh 2.5 times the command's.
--recovery-reward-scale 2.5
# BM's reading of StableMimic: 2.0 s (100 controls) of persisting target error stops a recovery episode, with
# "persisting" read by BM as consecutive controls; a 1.5 s (75-control) transition back to the command, with a linear
# weight as BM's choice.
--recovery-controls 100 75
